-- MineTools: the three tool families and their chest flagships, as data.
-- The ids below are save data: a player's owned tier is stored by id, so an
-- id is renamed only with a migration. Display names are free, and they were
-- reskinned away from the periodic-table ladder every mining game ships with.
--
-- GENERATED BY skills-src/gentools.js -- edit that, not this.
--
-- Shop tools are bought with COINS. Chest flagships are never sold and never
-- priced; they drop from named chests at the rates below. That firewall is what
-- keeps the mine -> coins -> packs loop from compounding.
--
-- Each family plays differently rather than just hitting harder:
--
--   pickaxe    aim one block, swing, break it. Reach 26.
--   drill      hold to mine continuously. Footprint is the trade -- a 3x3
--              clears nine cells but each one is softer than a 1x1's single
--              cell, because price buys throughput, not free width.
--   explosive  throw, blast, cooldown. Extra bombs split the power budget:
--              a three-pod cluster does NOT get single-bomb power three times.
--
-- The two equating rules, enforced by the generator:
--
--   drills      DCS = power x footprint_cells x rate
--   explosives  DC  = power x bombs x blocks_per_bomb
--
-- Both are PRE-CAP budgets. Damage above a block's remaining HP is discarded,
-- so a 5,700-power charge realises about fifteen per cell in zone 1. The
-- ladders only pay out at the depth they were priced for.
